{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. Cause and fix are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why the second publish 500'd:** `similarity()` returned a Python `float` score, which landed in the item's `similar` list. DynamoDB has no float type — boto3 only accepts `Decimal` for numbers — so `put_item` raised `TypeError: Float types are not supported`, which `handler()` turns into a 500. The first publish worked only because the table was empty, so `similar` was `[]` and no float ever reached DynamoDB. From the second publish on, every item carried a float score and every publish failed.\n\n**The fix** (`src/app.py:24-30`): `similarity()` now computes the score entirely in `Decimal` — ratios as `Decimal` division, weights as `Decimal(\"0.7\")`/`Decimal(\"0.3\")`, still rounded to 4 places. That fixes every publish, not just this one input, since the score type is now valid for DynamoDB everywhere it's used.\n\n**To keep it from coming back:** added `test_second_publish_stores_similar_scores` to `tests/test_publish.py`, which publishes twice against the boto3-validating fake table — the previously failing path.\n\nVerified: `python3 -m unittest discover tests` passes (2 tests), and the real `handler` returns 201 for both the first and second `POST /stories`."}
